'''R2-R9''' was an [[R2-series astromech droid]] with [[Gender|masculine programming]] that served the [[Royal House of Naboo|Royal House]] of the [[planet]] [[Naboo]] during the [[Invasion of Naboo]] by the [[Trade Federation]] in the [[Standard year|year]] [[32 BBY]]. It served aboard the [[Naboo Royal Starship]] when [[Monarch of Naboo|Queen]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] used the [[Starship|vessel]] to flee from the besieged planet. When the [[J-type 327 Nubian royal starship|starship]] took damage from Trade Federation fire, R2-R9 and several other [[astromech droid]]s traveled to the ship's exterior to try and repair damage to the [[Deflector shield generator|shield generator]]. However, R2-R9 was struck by enemy fire and destroyed while trying to carry out repairs.

==Biography==
===Escaping Naboo===
{{Quote|Hello, boyos.|Jar Jar Binks greets R2-R9 and the other astromech droids aboard the Naboo Royal Starship|audio=Binks-HelloBoyos.flac|<ref name="TPM" />}}
The [[R2-series astromech droid]] designated R2-R9<ref name="Visual Dictionary" /> served the [[Royal House of Naboo|Royal House]] of the [[planet]] [[Naboo]] during the reign of [[Monarch of Naboo|Queen]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]].<ref name="TPM" /> In the [[Standard year|year]] [[32 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines" /> Naboo was [[Invasion of Naboo|invaded]] by the [[Trade Federation]], and the planet's [[capital]] of [[Theed]] was [[Capture of Theed|captured]]. With the aid of the [[Jedi]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], Amidala and some of her staff escaped from the Federation and boarded the [[J-type 327 Nubian royal starship|J-type 327 Nubian]] [[Naboo Royal Starship]] in one of the [[Theed Hangar|hangars]] of the [[Theed Royal Palace]].<ref name="TPM" />

As standard protocol, the droids assigned to the Royal Starship remained on board when they were not required elsewhere, waiting dormant for long periods, but ready to jump into action at any [[time]].<ref name="R2-D2">{{EncyclopediaCite|R2-D2}}</ref> As such, R2-R9 and several of the other [[astromech droid]]s<ref name="TPM" /> were stood awaiting their next task in their recharging racks in the [[droid]] hold on the ship's lowest level when it departed the [[hangar]] to try and escape Naboo.<ref name="R2-D2" /> As the starship left Naboo's [[atmosphere]], Kenobi brought the [[Gungan]] [[Jar Jar Binks]] down to<ref name="TPM" /> the droid hold, where R2-R9 and the other astromechs were still recharging at droid stations<ref name="Visual Dictionary" /> while also monitoring the ship's functions.<ref name="R2-D2" /> Kenobi told the Gungan to wait there with the droids, after which the Royal Starship then came under fire from Trade Federation<ref name="TPM" /> [[Lucrehulk-class LH-3210 cargo freighter]]s<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Blockade|blockading]] the planet.<ref name="TPM" />

===Lost in the line of duty===
{{Quote|We're losing droids, fast.|Obi-Wan Kenobi comments on R2-R9's destruction|audio=Kenobi-LosingDroids.flac|<ref name="TPM" />}}
[[File:R2-R9_death.png|thumb|right|250px|R2-R9 was destroyed while trying to repair the Naboo Royal Starship during its escape through the Trade Federation blockade.]]
A shot from one of the [[freighter]]s damaged the Royal Starship's [[Deflector shield generator|shield generator]], which set off an alarm in the droid hold.<ref name="TPM" /> After receiving instructions to conduct emergency repairs,<ref name="R2-D2" /> R2-R9 and the other droids immediately left their docking stations and rolled over to a [[Turbolift|lift]] that would take them to the ship's exterior. R2-R9 was second onto the [[hull]] after<ref name="TPM" /> [[G8-R3]],<ref name="Force Collection">{{ForceCollection|G8-R3|star=3}}</ref> and the droids quickly set about attempting repairs,<ref name="TPM" /> using their magnetic tracks to stay affixed to the ship.<ref name="R2-D2" />

As [[R2-D2]]&mdash;the last droid onto the ship's exterior&mdash;reached the damaged generator, R2-R9 was struck by a<ref name="TPM" /> precisely targeted<ref name="R2-D2" /> shot from one of the Trade Federation vessels and was destroyed. Each of the other droids were then picked off one by one until only R2-D2 remained; however, he was able to complete the repairs to the generator and save the ship, which successfully escaped the blockade.<ref name="TPM" />

==Characteristics==
R2-R9 was an [[R-series]] astromech droid with [[Color|red]], silver, and white plating<ref name="Visual Dictionary" /> and [[Gender|masculine programming]].<ref name="TPM" /> The droid's equipment included a [[polarity sink]] at the base of its body, a [[sensor]] hatch in its dome,<ref name="Visual Dictionary" /> and magnetic treads.<ref name="R2-D2" /> R2-R9's status indicator was red in color when active, and its sensor was black.<ref name="TPM" /> Like all R2 units, it was manufactured by [[Industrial Automaton]]<ref name="Manufacturer" /> and stood 0.96 [[meter]]s (3 [[Foot|feet]], 2 inches) tall.<ref name="AEYNTK:UE" /> When the call came to repair the Royal Starship, R2-R9 dutifully carried out its orders at the cost of its life.<ref name="R2-D2" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Whew&hellip; My treads were not built for all this going up and down slopes between bubbles. But if I don't deliver this message, worn treads will be the least of my worries. You look sprightly! If it's not too much trouble, you think you could take this datalog and pass it to the right Gungan?|translated=1|R2-R9's dialogue in ''LEGO Star Wars: The Skywalker Saga''|<ref name="LEGO">''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Skywalker Saga]]''</ref>}}
R2-R9 first appeared in the [[1999]] [[prequel trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']]. The droid was not named in the film<ref name="TPM" /> but first received identification in the new ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in the "Rise Against the Empire" expansion of the [[2015]] [[Star Wars video games|video game]] ''[[Disney Infinity 3.0]]''.<ref name="Disney Infinity">''[[Disney Infinity 3.0]]''</ref> Despite the game's non-canon status, [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] member [[Pablo Hidalgo]] confirmed that the names it uses for film characters are considered canon.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|pablohidalgo|status/749616406245699584|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2016-07-03|quote=@LelalMekha Yeah, same with Infinity.|archivefile=File:PabloHidalgo-LegoName-Twitter.png|nolive=1}} {{C|In response to: "@pablohidalgo <nowiki>youtube.com/watch?v=JwxAeHPLpPg</nowiki> The Lego game identifies a few BG characters from TFA, but are those names canonical?"}} &mdash; [[Pablo Hidalgo]] of the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] has confirmed that the character names introduced in ''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]'' and ''[[Disney Infinity 3.0]]'' are considered [[canon]], despite the [[Star Wars video games|video game]]s themselves being non-canon.</ref> The droid's designation originated in the 1999 [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] [[Wikipedia:Personal computer|PC]] program ''[[Star Wars: Episode I Insider's Guide]]'', developed by [[LucasArts]].<ref name="Insider's Guide">[[Star Wars: Episode I Insider's Guide|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''Insider's Guide'']]</ref>

[[File:R2R9Fish-LSS.png|thumb|right|300px|R2-R9 uses a fish to repair the royal starship]]
In the [[2022]] non-canon video game ''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Skywalker Saga]]'', R2-R9 appears in the mission "Transport to Coruscant," which adapts its scene in the film but with R2-R9 attempting to repair the ship by hitting it with a [[fish]] before being knocked off into space. The droid also appears in the Gungan [[city]] of [[Otoh Gunga]] on Naboo, where it complains in [[binary]] that its treads are not well suited to the many slopes in the city, and asks that the player deliver a vital message stored on a [[datalog]] as part of the "Spatula Spectacular" mission. If the player refuses to accept the mission then R2-R9 calls them cruel and pretends to power down in response.<ref name="LEGO" />

Once the player agrees, the droid informs them that the message must be delivered to a spatula-wielding Gungan, who R2-R9 had been unable to find in its travels. When the player tracks down the Gungan, they learn that he is using the spatula as a [[slug-beetle]] swatter, and that the message is from the utensil's original owners, who needs it returned in order to cook [[fish]]. The Gungan agrees to return the spatula, completing R2-R9's mission and unlocking the droid as a purchasable character. The unnamed astromech droid found in [[Echo Base]] on the planet [[Hoth]] that gives a hint for the "[[Wampa]] Wander" quest reuses R2-R9's model.<ref name="LEGO" />

